/// A kinematic capsule walked by gameplay (blueprint §19.2d item 9, over Rapier's kinematic character controller). The entity's origin is the capsule's centre minus `center` — with the default `center` the origin is at the feet. Moved by `move`/`jump` commands (one `move` per tick; no command is standing still) or, with `move_action`/`jump_action` named, by the runtime itself from those actions (walking relative to the `fynkel.ThirdPersonCamera` that targets the entity, if any). Slopes up to `max_slope` are climbed, steeper ones slid down; steps up to `max_step_height` are climbed; gravity accumulates while airborne and the character snaps to ground within `snap_to_ground`. Ground contact, sliding and the effective velocity are held state (`characterState()`). Its own kinematic capsule replaces any `RigidBody`/`Collider` on the entity (`FYN-H0006`), collides by its object's `fynkel.Layer` and its `mask`, reports contact and trigger events and pushes dynamic bodies as a body of `mass` kilograms would.
